<tr><th class="News">08-29</th><td class="News"><a title="ReignOS is an Arch Linux-based gaming distribution. It boots into a graphical system installer which installs a base system, then downloads and installs all extra components after the first boot. The distribution offers a broad range of hardware compatibility by supporting various window compositors, including Steam's Gamescope, KDE's KWin, Wayland's Cage and Weston, and X.Org's X11. It also supports all popular GPUs (Intel, AMD, NVIDIA), as well as hybrid-graphics setups, mGPU and eGPU graphics processing units. ReignOS can boot into a standard KDE Plasma desktop, Steam gaming platform, or a custom-designed control centre that offers a choice user interface options." href="reignos">ReignOS</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">08-24</th><td class="News"><a title="LankeOS is an independent Chinese Linux distribution built using the Linux From Scratch (LFS) book. It is a live image that boots into a lightweight desktop powered by the Noctalia desktop shell on top of the niri Wayland compositor. It can be installed to a hard disk using a manual method. Besides niri, a separate binary package archive with KDE Plasma is also available for download and installation. The distribution uses a custom package manager called &quot;lpkg&quot; for installing new packages from source code, upgrading existing packages and removing superfluous software. LankeOS provides a complete Chinese desktop with out-of-the-box support for Simplified Chinese input using Noto Sans CJK fonts, although the project's website and documentation is also available in English." href="lankeos">LankeOS</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">08-23</th><td class="News"><a title="LajtLinux is a set of minimalist and lightweight Debian-based live images featuring several Wayland compositors and window managers. These include labwc, LXQt, Mango, niri, River, Sway and Wayfire. They are localised into the Polish language and offer a text-mode system installer, except for the LXQt variant which provides a choice of English or Polish languages and a graphical Debian Installer. The project's focus is to build Debian respins that are lightweight, simple, usable and low on resource usage." href="lajtlinux">LajtLinux</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">08-22</th><td class="News"><a title="Spaced Linux is a desktop Linux distribution based on Devuan's &quot;Unstable&quot; branch and featuring the MATE desktop environment on top of the Compiz compositing window manager. Like its parent, it uses the SysV init system. The distribution boots into a barebones live environment which offers the possibility to install Spaced Linux to a hard disk using the Calamares system installer. Once installed, a Welcome screen provides single-click options to extend the distribution by installing a collection of suggested applications (for web, office and multimedia use), adding SpacedBazaar (for Flatpak applications) or installing the NVIDIA graphics drivers. Spaced Linux intends to be modular, transparent and free of systemd, accessible to both beginners and advanced Linux users." href="spaced">Spaced Linux</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">08-21</th><td class="News"><a title="VasakOS is a desktop Linux distribution based on Arch Linux and featuring a custom-built Vasak desktop interface that runs on top of the Wayfire compositor. It is developed using Rust for core logic and Vue.js for a fluid and modern user interface, all orchestrated through the Tauri framework. The project's goal is to provide a clean, elegant and user-centric desktop with essential tools pre-installed." href="vasakos">VasakOS</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">08-20</th><td class="News"><a title="PolonOS is a Polish desktop Linux distribution based on Debian's &quot;Testing&quot; branch and featuring the KDE Plasma desktop. It is localised into Polish. The distribution includes a PolonOS Welcome assistant, the Calamares system installer, an automatic installer of popular drivers (including NVIDIA graphics and Broadcom wireless drivers), and an integrated application installer with support for Flatpak packages." href="polonos">PolonOS</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">08-19</th><td class="News"><a title="CobaltX is an Arch-based Linux distribution built specifically for gamers. It features the KDE Plasma desktop and comes pre-installed with the complete Linux gaming stack, i.e. Steam, Heroic Games Launcher, Bottles, Lutris, Wine, RetroArch, MangoHud and GameMode. It is built using the Archiso tool with a custom Calamares system installer. Under the hood, the distribution deploys the Linux Zen kernel for low-latency desktop performance. CobaltX also provides support for NVIDIA GPUs via a single-click installation option in the distribution's Welcome app." href="cobaltx">CobaltX</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">08-18</th><td class="News"><a title="CapivaraOS is a Brazilian desktop and server Linux distribution based on Fedora. It is available in three desktop editions - &quot;Marsh&quot; (KDE Plasma), &quot;Snout&quot; (GNOME) and &quot;Pup&quot; (Xfce), as well as a separate home server variant called &quot;HERD&quot;. All editions are localised into Brazilian Portuguese. The distribution uses the Anaconda system installer and includes many popular web, productivity and multimedia applications." href="capivaraos">CapivaraOS</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">08-16</th><td class="News"><a title="Mainstream Linux is an Arch-based Linux distribution with a highly customised desktop using the Quickshell toolkit on top of the Hyprland compositor. It includes a variety of user-friendly features, such a Material You desktop layout, per-workspace layout switching, a session restore option, a gaming mode, as well as a graphical settings tool to customise displays, themes, key bindings, networking and updates. The distribution uses the Calamares system installer with several install modes and applies automatic Btrfs snapshots before every update." href="mainstream">Mainstream OS</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">08-15</th><td class="News"><a title="SkillFishOS is a gaming-focused Linux distribution based on Debian's &quot;Unstable&quot; branch and featuring a themed KDE Plasma desktop. Originally developed for the AMD BC250 compact motherboard built around AMD's Cyan Skillfish accelerated processing unit (APU), it is also available for generic 64-bit personals computers. SkillFishOS ships with Steam, EmuDeck, ES-DE, Heroic and Proton gaming clients pre-installed. It also includes a tailored Linux kernel, pre-configured Btrfs snapshots, a steampunk-themed dark desktop, Unsloth Studio application designed to run and export open-source artificial intelligence (AI) models, and a remote control option. Besides gaming, the distribution is also suitable for emulation work, local AI and general desktop use." href="skillfishos">SkillFishOS</a></td></tr>
</table><br>
